<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jehoiachin</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as King Jehoiachin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jehoiachin was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> who surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a> in 597 BCE. He was deported to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> with the Judean elite. The episode shows the military reach of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jehoiachin.jpg" alt="Jehoiachin" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillaume Rouille · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jehoiachin-Jeconiah.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
